 "description": "BIGVILLE R7 (block 255000) -- the BANK ENTITY run by the banker AGENT Scrooge McBankFace (NOT a magic third party): funds SEPARATE from his personal coin. bf_accrue is INTEREST -- the cross-frame MULTIPLICATIVE base (CLAUDE.md invariant): balance' = IDiv(balance*(10000+rate_bp)+5000, 10000), round-half-up on integers via the pre-existing IDiv Term (NO new Rust, NO Round primitive), so rate_bp is INTENSIONAL (basis points, the cross-frame map) and the balance is OBSERVED STEPPED as INTEGER coin -- no float lives in a frame. bf_set_rate makes the rate Scrooge's decision_value (fair_rate_bp + greed_premium_bp) propagated to every issued mortgage. bf_salary transfers bank->Scrooge each cycle iff reserves>=salary>0 (his personal wealth tracks the salary, not the reserves; salary=0 is the ablation). bf_insolvent flags reserves<=0 -- a systemic event DISTINCT from Scrooge's personal wealth. Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
